DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
       This system call is obsolete.  Use uuttiimmeennssaatt(2) instead.

       The ffuuttiimmeessaatt() system  call  operates  in  exactly  the  same  way  as
       uuttiimmeess(2), except for the differences described in this manual page.

       If  _p_a_t_h  is relative, then it is interpreted relative to the directory
       referred to by the file descriptor _d_i_r_f_d (rather than relative  to  the
       current  working  directory  of  the  calling  process,  as  is done by
       uuttiimmeess(2) for a relative pathname).

       If _p_a_t_h is relative and _d_i_r_f_d is the special value AATT__FFDDCCWWDD, then  _p_a_t_h
       is interpreted relative to the current working directory of the calling
       process (like uuttiimmeess(2)).

       If  _p_a_t_h is absolute, then _d_i_r_f_d is ignored.  (See ooppeennaatt(2) for an ex‐
       planation of why the _d_i_r_f_d argument is useful.)

RREETTUURRNN VVAALLUUEE
       On success, ffuuttiimmeessaatt() returns a 0.  On error, -1 is returned and  _e_r_‐
       _r_n_o is set to indicate the error.

